<title>GERMANY: POLL- German July M3 money supply data.</title>
<headline>POLL- German July M3 money supply data.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>German M3 figures are expected to be published by the Bundesbank next week. Ten analysts were polled on Friday and gave the following forecasts. (Figures in percent). In June, M3 grew at a seasonally-adjusted, annualised rate of 6.4 percent compared with the fourth quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>ECONOMIST					     M3 growth vs Q4/96</p>
<p>Michael Schubert, Commerzbank, Frankfurt	    6.1</p>
<p>Petra Koehler, Dresdner Bank, Frankfurt	     6.0</p>
<p>Jens Kramer, Norddt. Landesbank, Hanover	    6.5</p>
<p>Ralf Kugelstadt, UBS, Frankfurt			 6.2</p>
<p>Irgeen Rust, Westdt. Landesbank, Duesseldorf	6.3</p>
<p>Klaus Papenbrock, DB Research, Frankfurt	    6.3</p>
<p>Eckhard Schulte, IBJ, Frankfurt			 6.5</p>
<p>Joerg Kraemer, Merrill Lynch, Frankfurt	     6.2</p>
<p>Timo Klein, MMS International, Frankfurt	    6.3</p>
<p>Lothar Hessler, TCM, Duesseldorf			6.3</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
